* Assert the passage-page state offsets against the struct at build time.

  The offsets the passage assembly indexes co_arch_state_stack_t with were
  hand-written hex strings sitting next to the fields they describe, with no
  check that the two agreed. Since this header is shared ABI between the host
  driver and the guest kernel, a field widened on one side without its offset
  updated desynchronises the assembly from the C declaration silently.

  Each offset now has a single numeric definition, stringified for the asm,
  and an assertion against __builtin_offsetof. A mismatch is a compile error.

